dsh-wallpaper README · What it does：- **Host half** (`lib/index.js`) registers a small API on the DSH web server:
  - `GET /dsh-wallpaper/config.json` — the settings file, plus the image's mtime;
  - `GET /dsh-wallpaper/image` — the image itself (jpg / jpeg / png / webp / avif / gif / svg);
  - `POST /dsh-wallpaper/config` — merge a patch into the settings (clamped to sane ranges);
  - `POST /dsh-wallpaper/upload` — store an uploaded photo (magic-byte check, 40 MB cap) and point the config at it.
- **Client half** (`lib/client.js`) injects one `<style>` element and paints the photo on `<html>` as a fixed background, then overrides five surface tokens with translucent versions of a neutral palette:
  `--dsw-alias-bg-base`, `--dsw-alias-bg-layer-1`, `--dsw-alias-bg-layer-2`, `--dsw-alias-bg-layer-3`, `--dsw-alias-bg-module-platform`.
  It also registers a **设置 → 背景壁纸** page, so the whole thing is driven from the GUI.

